    "raw_response": "```json\n{\n  \"inputs\": [\n    \"real_continuous_in\",\n    \"real_discrete_in\",\n    \"int_in\"\n  ],\n  \"outputs\": [\n    \"real_continuous_out\",\n    \"real_discrete_out\",\n    \"int_out\",\n    \"bool_out\"\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"This scenario probes the FMU behavior under different types of excitations. The input 'real_continuous_in' is driven by a step function, testing the response to a sudden change in the input. The 'real_discrete_in' is subjected to a ramp signal to observe the system's behavior under gradual increase. Finally, 'int_in' receives a sine wave excitation to evaluate the system's reaction to periodic inputs. Outputs include 'real_continuous_out' for continuous behavior, 'real_discrete_out' for the discrete output, and 'int_out' for integer-based behavior, along with 'bool_out' to capture the system’s logic-based response to the inputs.\"\n}\n```"
